---
const guarantees = [
  {
    label: "Review gates",
    body: "Every agent action proposes a change; a credentialed actuary accepts or rejects. No silent writes to a rate plan.",
  },
  {
    label: "Actuarial audit trail",
    body: "Each accepted change ties to the originating filing, the prompt, the model version, the reviewer, and the timestamp. SOX-aligned, ASOP-compliant, SERFF-traceable.",
  },
  {
    label: "Reproducible runs",
    body: "Every quote, every regression test, every model fit replays from the same inputs. Re-run an exam in two years and get the same answer.",
  },
];
---

<section class="bg-[var(--bg-panel)] border-y border-[var(--rule)]">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1180px] px-6 md:px-10 py-24">
    <div class="max-w-[760px]">
      <p class="eyebrow mb-5">Control plane</p>
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-[2.25rem] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.012em]">
        Every agent runs on a control plane built for actuaries
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[1.0625rem] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--fg-muted)]">
        Tesora agents do not act unilaterally. Every change is proposed, reviewed, and recorded. The substrate is the same one a chief actuary would build if they had unlimited engineering time: a single graph of filings, raters, exposures, and quotes, with every edit lineage-tracked.
      </p>
    </div>

    <dl class="mt-16 grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-10 md:gap-12">
      {guarantees.map((g) => (
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-[1.125rem] tracking-tight">{g.label}</dt>
          <dd class="mt-3 text-[0.95rem] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--fg-muted)]">{g.body}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>
